## Scope: the MIT grant above covers this plugin's original code only

The three bundled data assets and the third-party dependencies retain their own
licenses.

- **NMRShiftDB2-derived HOSE shift statistics** are a derivative database under
  the **nmrshiftdb2 Database License (ODbL-derived)**. The source file is
  `src/providers/ocl/nmrshiftdb2.database.json`. The package embeds the data in
  `nmrWorker-*.js` and `GnnShiftPredictor-*.js` at the ZIP root. The license
  permits commercial use and requires share-alike and attribution on
  redistribution, including redistribution of the plugin ZIP. See
  `src/providers/ocl/NMRSHIFTDB2_LICENSE.md` for provenance and the license text.

- **NMRShiftDB2-derived GNN shift model weights and training-domain counts**
  are offered under the same **nmrshiftdb2 Database License (ODbL-derived)**,
  not under MIT. The source files are `src/providers/gnn/model/1H.fp16.onnx`,
  `src/providers/gnn/model/13C.fp16.onnx` and `src/providers/gnn/model/domain.json`.
  The package ships the weights as `1H.fp16-*.onnx` and `13C.fp16-*.onnx` at the
  ZIP root and embeds the domain counts in `nmrWorker-*.js` and
  `GnnShiftPredictor-*.js`. See `src/providers/ocl/NMRSHIFTDB2_LICENSE.md`.

- **Ilm-NMR-P31-derived ³¹P HOSE shift statistics** are derived from Ilm-NMR-P31
  v3.0 (Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20762603), which is licensed under
  **CC BY 4.0** (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). About 27,000 of
  its 43,317 entries come from NMRexp (Wang and Zhu, Zenodo DOI
  10.5281/zenodo.17296666, **CC BY 4.0**). The values were filtered and
  transformed into aggregated HOSE statistics. The GitHub copy the table was
  built from carries a **BSD-3-Clause** license, copyright (c) 2026 Robert
  Geitner, and that credit is kept; the data is redistributed with the author's
  permission (owner, 2026-11-20). The source file is
  `src/providers/ocl/ilm-nmr-p31.database.json`. The package embeds the data in
  `nmrWorker-*.js` and `GnnShiftPredictor-*.js` at the ZIP root. See
  `src/providers/ocl/ILM_NMR_P31_LICENSE.md` for the attribution and license text.

- **Third-party dependencies** — openchemlib (BSD-3-Clause), zod (MIT),
  onnxruntime-web 1.22.0 (MIT, Microsoft; shipped as `ort.wasm.bundle.min-*.js`,
  `ort-wasm-simd-threaded-*.mjs` and `ort-wasm-simd-threaded-*.wasm`) — remain
  under their own terms. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

Nothing in the MIT grant above conveys any right to those materials beyond their
respective licenses.

MIT was chosen deliberately rather than as a default: the nmrshiftdb2 Database
License requires that prediction software relying on the database be under an
OSI-approved license. MIT is OSI-approved and satisfies that condition.
